==================== Input ====================
// A blank line travels with the entry it preceded.
//
// Blank-line preservation normally measures the source gap between two adjacent entries, which says
// nothing once entries move. The fact is captured per entry in source order before permuting.
//
// `/travels`: the blank precedes `summary`, and follows it to its new position.
// `/to-front`: the blank precedes `operationId`, which ordering moves to first. There is no preceding
// entry to separate it from, so it is dropped.
// `/before-comma`: the blank sits before the comma, so it separates nothing and is not a blank line
// between two entries at all. It must be counted exactly as the unpermuted separator counts it --
// which is to say, not at all. Counting raw newlines in the gap instead would invent a blank here,
// and would still be idempotent, so only this shape catches it.
{
  "openapi": "3.0.0",
  "paths": {
    "/travels": {
      "get": {
        "responses": {},

        "summary": "s",
        "operationId": "op"
      }
    },
    "/to-front": {
      "get": {
        "responses": {},

        "operationId": "op"
      }
    },
    "/before-comma": {
      "get": {
        "responses": {}

        ,
        "summary": "s",
        "operationId": "op"
      }
    }
  }
}

==================== Output ====================
------------------
{ printWidth: 80 }
------------------
// A blank line travels with the entry it preceded.
//
// Blank-line preservation normally measures the source gap between two adjacent entries, which says
// nothing once entries move. The fact is captured per entry in source order before permuting.
//
// `/travels`: the blank precedes `summary`, and follows it to its new position.
// `/to-front`: the blank precedes `operationId`, which ordering moves to first. There is no preceding
// entry to separate it from, so it is dropped.
// `/before-comma`: the blank sits before the comma, so it separates nothing and is not a blank line
// between two entries at all. It must be counted exactly as the unpermuted separator counts it --
// which is to say, not at all. Counting raw newlines in the gap instead would invent a blank here,
// and would still be idempotent, so only this shape catches it.
{
  "openapi": "3.0.0",
  "paths": {
    "/travels": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "op",

        "summary": "s",
        "responses": {}
      }
    },
    "/to-front": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "op",
        "responses": {}
      }
    },
    "/before-comma": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "op",
        "summary": "s",
        "responses": {}
      }
    }
  }
}

